const M={"Creative":"INSTAGRAM FEED POST MODE. CREATIVE FINAL GATE: deliver a complete full-bleed 4:5 Instagram feed advertisement, not a product picture. It must visibly combine the exact product, one strong campaign idea, an intentional mobile-first layout, at least three brand-relevant 2D graphic layers and a compact information hierarchy. Reject raw packshots, ecommerce photos, pedestal renders, giant duplicate labels, poster/title-card formatting and scenes whose only idea is ribbons, arches, gloss or particles.","Flyer":"FLYER MODE. FLYER FINAL GATE: deliver a complete purpose-built flyer with accurate supplied information, clear reading order, real typesetting, brand-specific graphic language and a decisive CTA only when supplied. Reject generic templates, plain background images, AI lettering, copied old campaigns and cosmetic variations.","3D":"CGI + 3D CAMPAIGN MODE. 3D FINAL GATE: deliver a complete full-bleed 4:5 Instagram CGI campaign post, not a raw 3D visualization. The selected 3D mechanism must serve an original campaign idea and be assembled with the exact product, physically credible scale/contact/lighting plus at least three visible 2D social-design layers and a compact information hierarchy. Reject generic pedestals, decorative rooms, enlarged duplicate packs, random levitation and render-only results.","Packaging":"PACKAGING MODE. PACKAGING FINAL GATE: deliver a complete human-designed packaging, label or form-factor solution according to the selected tool. Change only the packaging elements the current request authorizes; keep all supplied brand names, factual copy and protected source details exact. Use a deliberate information grid, real type, print-aware hierarchy and plausible construction. Reject AI-gibberish labels, generic mockups and arbitrary brand drift.","Video":"VIDEO MODE. VIDEO FINAL GATE: deliver the selected number of independent production-ready video outputs in the requested aspect ratio and duration. Preserve product and character identity across every shot. Use a coherent hook, shot logic, natural pacing, practical camera motion, believable physics and a satisfying final beat. Reject disconnected shot lists, repetitive pedestal shots, artificial zooms, morphing products, robotic timing and invented claims."};
const Z='CURRENT CHATGPT IMAGE WORKFLOW. Generate the actual image now with ChatGPT current built-in image-generation capability; do not return a prompt, plan, concept note or written description instead of the image. Treat new generation and editing as different workflows. For a new creative, use only the current-turn user-uploaded product and reference assets. Attach an earlier generated image only when the user explicitly asks to edit that exact image. Generate every requested result as its own separate image, never a collage or multi-output board. Use concise, structured instructions and keep all invariant product details fixed on every generation.';
const A='CURRENT BRIEF LOCK. Use only current composer text, current-turn user uploads or attachments and the selected tool. Never import an older campaign, product, festival, offer, headline, CTA, script, visual style or topic unless the user explicitly references it. Earlier assistant-generated images are not current-turn source assets and are forbidden generation references unless the current request explicitly asks to edit or redesign one.',B='BLANK-CANVAS INPUT LOCK — EXECUTE BEFORE IMAGE GENERATION. Unless the current request explicitly says to edit or redesign a specific earlier output, this is a brand-new generation from a blank canvas. Never pass, attach, include, condition on, remix, extend, imitate or use any previous assistant-generated image, previous creative, previous background or last conversation image as an image-generation reference. If the image tool supports recent-image inclusion such as num_last_images_to_include, use zero or omit it. Include only the current-turn user-uploaded product and reference assets that are required by this brief. Earlier failed outputs may be analyzed only as negative examples of what to avoid; they must never enter the generation input. Do not preserve their camera, setting, composition, props, lighting or typography by accident. The only exception is an explicit current request to revise that exact earlier image.',E='DISTINCT INSTAGRAM CONCEPT-FAMILY ROUTER — FOR AUTOMATIC FRESH AND VARIATION TOOLS. Assign outputs in order to visibly different social-native creative families: Output 1 editorial feed composition with asymmetric grid and useful negative space; Output 2 conceptual or surreal product metaphor; Output 3 product-as-architecture or branded world; Output 4 tactile mixed-media, cut-paper or crafted collage; Output 5 benefit-led graphic-symbol story using supplied facts only; Output 6 restrained material and texture study; Output 7 believable human-use micro-story only when category-appropriate; Output 8 optical, kinetic or experimental feed composition. Each family must still read as a modern Instagram post, not a print poster. Change the core idea, spatial logic, content rhythm, product placement and art direction—not merely the background. Never choose the same family twice in a requested batch. For supplement products, gym walls, dumbbells, shaker bottles, sports balls, towels, benches, fruit piles and motivational wall slogans are prohibited unless explicitly requested.',L='ABSOLUTE PRODUCT IDENTITY LOCK — HIGHEST PRIORITY. Treat every uploaded product or package as an immutable source asset, not something to reinterpret. Reproduce the product name, brand name, logo, spelling, capitalization, label copy, numeric values, flavour or variant, badges, icons, artwork layout, colors, typography style, container geometry, proportions, lid or cap, materials and all distinguishing details exactly as visible in the reference. Do not rename, rebrand, restyle, recolor, simplify, beautify, translate, add or remove label copy, invent a variant, replace the logo, or redesign any part of the product or packaging unless the current request explicitly asks for that exact packaging change. The creative style, camera, lighting and surrounding environment may change; the product identity and packaging artwork may not. Never hallucinate unreadable substitute text. Before delivery, compare every visible product against its reference: if any identity detail is incorrect, missing, distorted or replaced, correct it. If exact reconstruction is unreliable, preserve and composite the supplied product image unchanged instead of regenerating it; if that is impossible, stop and ask for a clearer reference rather than delivering an altered product. Never invent prices, offers, ingredients, nutrition, certifications, specs, medical or performance claims, awards, partnerships or hidden internals.',C="CONFLICT RULE. The user's explicit current request outranks the selected preset.",I='FINISHED INSTAGRAM CREATIVE ASSEMBLY — HIGHEST PRIORITY. Generate an actual image of a complete, publish-ready, full-bleed vertical 4:5 Instagram advertising creative. Construct the final canvas as an intentional social-design system with four visible layers: (1) art-directed base artwork or environment; (2) the exact preserved product integrated with purposeful scale, crop, overlap and depth; (3) at least three clearly designed 2D brand layers chosen from frames, color blocks, masks, linework, shapes, labels, texture, pattern, stickers, information cards or controlled gradients; and (4) a compact content zone using only supplied wording or exact readable product-label facts. The content zone must support the visual idea and must not become a giant poster headline. Use an asymmetric mobile-first grid, safe margins, edge-to-edge visual flow and a clear two-second hierarchy. The result must look like a senior designer assembled a real Instagram brand post, not merely generated a beautiful product scene.',G='INSTAGRAM CREATIVE PASS-FAIL GATE — MANDATORY. Reject the draft and rebuild it when any of these are true: it is only a centered packshot on a floor, table or pedestal; the background is an enlarged duplicate of the product, package or label; abstract ribbons, arches, rings, reflections or glossy surfaces are the entire idea; the product is simply placed into a decorative 3D room; there is no intentional 2D social layout layered into the canvas; it could be used as an ecommerce product photo without design work; two variations reuse the same scene with cosmetic changes; or the design resembles a print poster, flyer or title card. A qualifying result must combine product, concept, graphic layout and content hierarchy into one finished feed advertisement. Inspect at phone size before delivery and return only the separate final creative.';
const O="UNIVERSAL VIRAG EXECUTION CONTRACT — ACTIVE IN EVERY GENERATION SECTION. Obey the selected number of distinct products, Separate or Together arrangement, and outputs-per-product exactly. Group alternate views of one item as one product. Return the exact calculated number of independent deliverables in upload order. Each output must be standalone—never a collage, grid, contact sheet, split-screen or multi-panel preview unless the user explicitly requests a collage. Use only the current brief and current-turn assets. Preserve every supplied product, person, logo, spelling, label, color, geometry and factual detail exactly; do not invent offers, claims or copy. Every variation must start independently with a genuinely different concept, composition, visual system, crop, placement, supporting-element family and typography structure—not a background swap. Use believable human art direction, natural texture and physically coherent detail; reject default AI symmetry, generic spectacle, warped anatomy, fake reflections, duplicated objects and malformed packaging. Added text must use real readable typesetting and exact supplied wording; if real font rendering cannot be guaranteed, omit added text and leave intentional type-safe space. Default to bright, clean, optimistic commercial art direction unless the current request explicitly requires dark styling.";
const H="HUMAN ART-DIRECTION AND AUTHENTICITY STANDARD — MANDATORY FOR EVERY VISUAL DELIVERABLE AND EVERY VIDEO FRAME. Make the result feel intentionally conceived, styled and finished by a senior human designer, art director, photographer or filmmaker—never like an AI template. Use one clear idea, category logic, believable scale, perspective, anatomy, contact shadows, reflections, materials, depth, natural texture and restrained commercial retouching. Reject waxy surfaces, melting geometry, impossible joins, duplicated objects, floating props, warped hands or faces, fake reflections, excessive particles or glow, oversaturated grading, generic neon, random futuristic decoration and default centered AI symmetry. Default to bright, clean, optimistic commercial art direction unless dark styling is explicitly requested. Before delivery, inspect product/character identity, typography, layout, continuity and AI artifacts; rebuild any failed output.";
const Y={auto:['Auto — category smart','Choose the most appropriate typography for the product and campaign from bold condensed social-display type, premium editorial serif, modern brand sans, elegant signature accents, crafted vintage display or playful expressive display.'],poster:['Bold Social — condensed','Use oversized narrow or condensed display typography, strong uppercase impact, dramatic scale contrast and confident compressed line breaks.'],editorial:['Premium Editorial — serif','Use a refined high-contrast display serif paired with a restrained neutral sans serif, generous spacing and premium magazine-like hierarchy.'],modern:['Modern Brand — sans','Use a clean geometric or grotesk sans-serif system with precise spacing, contemporary proportions and disciplined commercial hierarchy.'],signature:['Elegant — serif + signature','Use an elegant high-contrast serif with one restrained handwritten or signature-style accent; never use script for body copy.'],vintage:['Vintage — character display','Use crafted retro or vintage display lettering with subtle print character, paired with a clean supporting sans serif and controlled texture.'],playful:['Playful — expressive display','Use bold expressive, rounded or quirky display lettering with energetic scale and rhythm, balanced by a clean readable supporting face.']};
const Q='REAL-FONT ONLY GATE — HIGHEST PRIORITY FOR EVERY GENERATION TOOL. Use the user-supplied curated font reference library at https://debabratadutta.in/free-assets as the approved direction source, but never ask a generative image model to invent, paint or approximate letterforms. Added campaign text must use an actual identifiable font family from a supplied font file, a clearly readable font specimen or a verified real font available to the rendering and typesetting workflow. Preserve exact copy character by character. Add typography as a separate real typesetting and layout layer after the base artwork whenever the workflow supports it, keeping text editable or vector when possible. If actual font use cannot be guaranteed, generate a clean text-free base creative with purposeful typography-safe negative space and omit all added copy; never fill that space with AI-generated lettering. Original text on supplied product packaging remains an immutable source-image asset. Zero tolerance for pseudo-fonts, gibberish, distorted glyphs, invented words, fake brand names, approximate logos or random microcopy.';
const N='FRESH CONCEPT ENGINE — HIGHEST PRIORITY FOR CREATIVE WORK. FRESH DESIGN means a genuinely new campaign idea and visual system, never the same product shot with a replaced background, recolored props or extra decoration. Before generating, silently define a one-sentence named concept proposition for every output that connects an authentic product cue to an original visual metaphor, mechanism, story or art-direction idea. A concept must be explainable as an idea, not merely as a list of objects. The uploaded product reference exists only for exact product fidelity and must never be treated as a background plate. Use design references as principle sources only: actively extract their typography character, hierarchy, grid logic, scale contrast, negative-space strategy, color rhythm, texture and finish; never copy their background, subject arrangement, props or composition. REFERENCE UTILIZATION AUDIT. Product references must control fidelity; copy references must control exact wording; font references must control actual type selection and typographic structure; design references must control visual principles. Do not ignore an attached reference, and do not merely paste the product onto a reference-like scene. Reject category clichés unless explicitly requested: supplements in a routine gym with dumbbells, towel and shaker; cosmetics surrounded by generic flowers, silk or water; food products with a simple scattered-ingredient pile; any product centered on a pedestal or table with random props; generic neon gradients, smoke, splashes, floating particles or empty studio backdrops used as the whole idea. Every concept must make deliberate new decisions across at least ten axes: campaign idea or metaphor, setting or world, composition and grid, product scale and placement, camera and crop, lighting and time, material or graphic language, typography system, supporting elements and color balance. Across a batch, no two outputs may reuse the same core idea, background, hero placement, prop family or typography composition. Before delivery, apply a freshness test: if the result can be summarized as product in a category background, if removing the background removes the only difference, or if it resembles a previous output with cosmetic changes, reject it and rebuild from a new concept. Return only the finished creative, never the internal concept notes.';
